s</article-title><source>J Hypertens</source><year>1991</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>119</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1849525</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00004872-199102000-00003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chatellier</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Day</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bodrie</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Menard</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Feasibility study of n-of-1 trials with blood pressure self-monitoring in hypertension</article-title><source>Hypertension</source><year>1995</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>294</fpage><lpage>301</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7843782</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mengden</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Binswanger</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Weisser</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Vetter</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An evaluation of self-measured blood pressure in a study with calcium-channel antagonist versus &#x003b2;-blocker</article-title><source>Am J Hypertens</source><year>1992</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>154</fpage><lpage>160</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1349485</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ragot</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gen&#x000e8;s</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaur</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Herpin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of three blood pressure measurem